<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Normans</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-Normans were the medieval descendants of the Normans who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> after the conquest of 1066, together with the French-speaking aristocracy they formed there. From 1169 Anglo-Norman lords, invited by the deposed Leinster king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diarmait-mac-murchada">Diarmait Mac Murchada</a>, invaded Ireland, and Henry II's arrival in 1171 began English royal lordship over the island. They built castles, founded towns and took much of the east and south from Irish kings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-normans.jpg" alt="Anglo-Normans" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: by Albert Kretschmer, painters and costumer to the Royal Court Theatre, Berin, and Dr. Carl Rohrbach. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1000-1100,_Norman._-_033_-_Costumes_of_All_Nations_(1882).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
